003–2025; it shows what changed, not why. The record is 23 years long, shorter than the 30 years usually used to describe a climate. AIRS sees mostly clear and partly cloudy skies, and its global water-vapour trend is much smaller than MERRA-2's (about +0.1 vs +0.5 kg/m² per decade, 2003–2025); treat this trend as not yet confirmed."}}